  "raw": {
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Psychology_JREQ-002700": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities at Endicott College is currently seeking individuals to teach the following in-person courses in the Spring 2027 semester, with classes starting on January 25, 2027 and ending on May 14, 2027:  Psychology (PSY) 322 Biological Psychology Psychology (PSY) 345 Cognitive Psychology Compensation Per Course: In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course. This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses are taught in-person:  In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday/Wednesday/Friday 50-minute format or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-minute format. PSY 489 meets once a week on Fridays for an 85-minute block. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Marketing_JREQ-002699": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities at Endicott College is currently seeking individuals to teach one or more of the following in-person courses in the Spring 2027 semester, with classes starting on January 25, 2027 and ending on May 14, 2027:  Marketing Communication/Advertising (MCA) 312 Strategic Media Planning Students learn the planning process used to develop a marketing campaign. Utilizing research and data, students develop effective marketing planning. After studying case studies of real-world strategic marketing and media plans, students develop, present, and defend their own strategic marketing and media plans based on specific marketing objectives. The course emphasizes creative problem solving with hands-on group work that simulates a real-world work environment. Communication (CMM) 380 Media Ethics This course provides an overview of the ethical conflicts faced in contemporary society by media professionals. Through the application of various ethical frameworks, students consider the traditional and contemporary problems of expression and dissemination of information in a converged world. Communication (CMM) 306 Social Impact of the Media This course examines the role of media in modern culture. Students examine how media potentially impacts the development of beliefs, attitudes and behavior.  Students additionally engage in complicated examinations of media texts and their connections to appropriate political, social, and economic issues. Compensation Per Course: In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course. This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses are taught in-person:   In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday/Wednesday/Friday 50-minute format or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-minute format. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--School-of-Business_JREQ-002684": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Reporting to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business, the Associate Dean provides academic and operational leadership for the School’s undergraduate programs. Working collaboratively with the Dean, faculty, and administrative staff, the Associate Dean promotes academic quality, effective program delivery, and student success.   Responsibilities include academic assessment and reporting; course scheduling; recruitment, hiring, and supervision of full-time and part-time faculty; and oversight of administrative functions supporting undergraduate academic programs, advising, and student success. The Associate Dean supervises designated administrative staff and oversees several professionals who, in turn, lead La Chanterelle, Endicott’s teaching restaurant and experiential learning classroom.   The Associate Dean collaborates across disciplines and College offices to strengthen the undergraduate student experience. In partnership with the Dean, the role identifies emerging trends in business and higher education and translates them into program improvements and initiatives supporting recruitment, retention, and timely degree completion. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .    Key Responsibilities Associate Dean, Undergraduate Programs Reporting to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business, the Associate Dean provides academic and operational leadership for undergraduate programs, advancing academic quality, effective program delivery, and student success.   Academic Leadership and Program Operations - 25% ·         Oversee undergraduate course scheduling and program delivery. ·         Lead academic assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement. ·         Collaborate with the Dean to identify emerging trends in business and higher education and translate them into program improvements. ·         Use Workday to access and analyze academic and student data, prepare reports, and inform planning and decision-making. ·         Support budget planning and monitor expenditures within assigned areas in collaboration with the Dean.   Student Advising and Success - 20% ·         Oversee administrative functions supporting undergraduate academic programs, advising, and student success. ·         Collaborate across College offices to support recruitment, retention, and timely degree completion. ·         Address student academic concerns in partnership with faculty and appropriate College offices.   Faculty Leadership and Supervision - 25% ·         Recruit, hire, supervise, and support full-time and part-time faculty. ·         Coordinate faculty teaching assignments and promote effective instruction and professional development. ·         Foster a collaborative environment with clear expectations and accountability.   Administrative Leadership - 15% ·         Demonstrated experience supervising faculty or professional staff, setting expectations, supporting development, and addressing performance concerns. ·         Promote effective processes, communication, and collaboration across academic and administrative functions.   Community Engagement - 5% ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. ·  As part of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement.   Collective Bargaining Agreement and Policy - 5% ·         Develop and maintain a thorough understanding of the faculty collective bargaining agreement. ·         Apply relevant contract provisions and College policies to faculty assignments, workload, evaluation, and other supervisory responsibilities. ·         Consult with the Dean and Human Resources on contract interpretation and implementation.   La Chanterelle - A Non-Traditional Teaching Classroom/On-Campus Restaurant - 5% ·         Provide supervisory oversight of La Chanterelle’s management team, which leads daily operations, and support alignment with the School’s academic and experiential learning goals   Other Duties ·         Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure This position reports to and works under the general supervision of the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business.   Supervisory Responsibilities Direct reports include full-time and part-time undergraduate instructional faculty and designated staff supporting academic operations, student success and advising, and hospitality operations; internship faculty report directly to the Dean.   Core Competencies ●       Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. ●       Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. ●       Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. ●       Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and do things differently. ●       Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. ●       Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. ●       Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. ●       Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills ●        Master’s degree required; doctorate preferred ●        Minimum of 8 years in higher education or a related professional setting and that experience must be relevant to academic leadership or program administration ●        Former supervisory experience required ●        Strategic planning ●        Clear written and verbal communication skills ●        Experience in conflict resolution ●        Familiarity using Workday or a comparable higher education student information system to access and analyze academic data, generate reports, and support academic planning and student success. ●        Curriculum development and assessment experience preferred ●        Student advising and retention planning ●        Interprets data accurately, identifies trends, and uses evidence to guide decisions. ●        Collective bargaining agreement interpretation skills ●        Understands protocols when handling confidential matters ●        On occasion, ability to work an evening or weekend.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $131,000–$165,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: October 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Advising-Coordinator---Graduate-Instruction_JREQ-002658": {
      "title": "Advising Coordinator & Graduate Instruction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Advising Coordinator & Graduate Instruction serves a dual role supporting student success through academic advising and graduate-level instruction. Reporting to the Assistant Dean of Advising and Credentialing, this position provides direct academic advising to assigned students, serves as a Core Advisor to support and guide Academic Advisors, and contributes to the development and continuous improvement of advising practices within the Institute for Applied Behavioral Science.   In addition, the position provides graduate-level instruction and thesis support within the MS program. The individual will work closely with the Assistant Dean of Research and Thesis Coordinator to support students throughout the thesis process, including providing additional academic support, assisting with thesis-related activities, and participating in thesis defenses as needed.   The position includes an instructional in-load of five thesis course sections and requires strong knowledge of applied behavior analysis, graduate education, academic advising, research, and thesis development. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .   Key Responsibilities Academic Advising and Advising Coordination (50%) ·         Serve as an Academic Advisor and maintain regular communication with assigned advisees regarding academic progress, program requirements, performance, and overall student success. ·         Conduct an annual, in-depth synchronous advising and evaluation meeting with each assigned advisee, along with multiple points of contact throughout each semester, including synchronous meetings as appropriate. ·         Serve as a Core Advisor by providing guidance, support, information, and professional expertise to a designated group of Academic Advisors. ·         Provide consultation and support to Academic Advisors regarding student needs, academic planning, advising practices, and program requirements. ·         Attend annual academic planning meetings for students assigned to Academic Advisors within the Core Advisor structure. ·         Collaborate with the Assistant Dean of Advising and Credentialing to develop resources, tools, and support structures that strengthen the advising experience. ·         Assist with the onboarding and training of new Academic Advisors. ·         Contribute to the assessment and continuous improvement of advising practices and the overall student advising experience. ·         Identify student concerns and, when appropriate, connect students with relevant institutional resources and support services. ·         Maintain accurate and timely advising records and documentation. ·         Collaborate with faculty, staff, and academic leadership to promote student progression, engagement, and success.   Graduate Instruction and Thesis Support (50%) ·         Teach an instructional in-load of five thesis course sections within the MS program. ·         Provide graduate-level instruction, mentoring, and academic support to students enrolled in thesis courses. ·         Support students across the three thesis course experiences, including providing additional guidance to students who require assistance progressing through their thesis work. ·         Collaborate with the Assistant Dean of Research and Thesis Coordinator on thesis-related activities, student support, and program needs. ·         Assist with thesis defense preparation and participate in thesis defense coverage as needed. ·         Provide feedback and guidance to students regarding thesis development, research methodology, literature reviews, academic writing, and related research activities. ·         Support students in applying principles of applied behavior analysis and research methodology to their thesis projects. ·         Collaborate with faculty and academic leadership to promote high-quality graduate instruction and successful completion of thesis requirements. ·         Maintain appropriate instructional records and fulfill all responsibilities associated with assigned graduate courses. ·         Other duties as assigned   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Supervisory Responsibilities ·         No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ·         PhD in Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) or a closely related field, as appropriate to the program requirements. ·         Active Board-Certified Behavior Analyst–Doctoral (BCBA-D) certification. ·         Professional experience in academic advising and graduate-level instruction in higher education. ·         Demonstrated experience conducting systematic literature reviews. ·         Demonstrated experience with experimental research methodology in applied behavior analysis. ·         Strong knowledge of applied behavior analysis principles, research methodology, and graduate-level academic expectations. ·         Excellent written and oral communication skills. ·         Demonstrated ability to advise, mentor, and support graduate students effectively. ·         Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and deadlines. ·         Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and academic leadership. ·         Demonstrated commitment to student success, academic quality, and continuous improvement.   Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience advising graduate students in an ABA or related graduate program. ·         Experience teaching graduate-level thesis or research courses. ·         Experience mentoring students through the thesis or culminating research project process. ·         Experience participating in thesis defenses or graduate research evaluation. ·         Experience supporting or training academic advisors.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $65,000–$74,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Director--Organizational-Behavior-Science---Doctoral-Program_JREQ-002659": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Organizational Behavior Science - Doctoral Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Director of the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program supports the academic administration, development, and ongoing operations of the doctoral program within the Institute for Applied Behavioral Science. Reporting to the Dean, the Assistant Director provides leadership and coordination in doctoral student advising and mentorship, academic programming, research development, teaching, scholarship, and professional engagement.   The Assistant Director serves as a key academic resource for doctoral students throughout their progression in the program, including comprehensive examinations, research development, Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes, dissertation preparation, publication development, and professional presentations. The position also contributes to the broader priorities of the Institute and College through teaching, scholarship, committee service, community engagement, and external relationship development.   The Assistant Director will teach four courses annually, at least three of which will be at the doctoral level; advise and mentor a minimum of nine doctoral students; support doctoral student research and professional development; participate in dissertation and academic committees; and contribute to program, department, and College initiatives as assigned. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .   Key Responsibilities   Doctoral Student Advising, Mentorship & Academic Progress (40%) ·         Advise and mentor a minimum of nine doctoral students throughout their academic progression and professional development. ·         Serve as dissertation chair or committee member for assigned doctoral students, including reviewing dissertation proposals and drafts and participating in proposal and defense meetings. ·         Support and evaluate doctoral student readiness for comprehensive examinations in collaboration with appropriate program faculty. ·         Meet individually with assigned doctoral students on a weekly or biweekly basis, as appropriate to student needs and program milestones. ·         Facilitate weekly or biweekly research labs for assigned doctoral students. ·         Provide discipline-specific guidance regarding degree requirements, research development, professional development, and career preparation. ·         Review and support the development of IRB applications and research protocols. ·         Review and support students in developing manuscripts, publications, conference presentations, and other professional dissemination. ·         Help students identify and pursue professional development opportunities aligned with their academic, research, and career goals.   Teaching, Research & Scholarship (30%) ·         Teach four courses annually, at least three of which will be at the doctoral level. The remaining course may support departmental or programmatic needs, including master's-level instruction. ·         Develop and deliver high-quality instruction grounded in current research and evidence-based practices in organizational behavior science. ·         Maintain current knowledge of research, scholarship, and professional practices relevant to organizational behavior science, business, leadership, and related fields. ·         Engage in scholarly and professional dissemination through publications, conference presentations, invited presentations, podcasts, webinars, and other appropriate professional forums. ·         Contribute to research and scholarly initiatives within the Institute and support doctoral student engagement in research and dissemination activities. ·         Apply appropriate research methodologies, including single-subject and group experimental designs, to academic and applied research.   Program Administration & Development (15%) ·         Support the Dean in the ongoing administration, development, and continuous improvement of the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program. ·         Contribute to the development and implementation of program initiatives that enhance doctoral student learning, research, professional development, and overall student experience. ·         Identify opportunities to strengthen curriculum, academic programming, student support, and professional engagement. ·         Collaborate with faculty and staff to address programmatic needs and support effective communication and coordination. ·         Participate in doctoral program orientation, graduation, and other key academic milestones. ·         Support program-related projects and initiatives as assigned by the Dean.   Departmental & Institutional Service (10%) ·         Serve on department, school, and College committees as requested. ·         Participate in departmental, school-wide, and College-sponsored conferences, academic events, and professional development activities. ·         Participate in College-wide events and activities that support the student experience and broader College community, including Commencement, Homecoming, orientation, and other institutional events as appropriate. ·         Collaborate with colleagues across the Institute and College to advance shared academic and institutional priorities. ·         Participate in faculty and staff meetings and other activities necessary to support effective program and departmental operations.   External Engagement & Partnerships (5%) ·         Support the Director of Practicum and Immersion Experiences in developing and maintaining relationships with organizations and professionals in the business and applied behavioral science communities. ·         Help identify opportunities for doctoral students to engage in immersions, applied projects, research, professional development, and other experiential learning opportunities. ·         Represent the Institute and the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program professionally with external organizations, community partners, and industry professionals. ·         Contribute to the development of partnerships that strengthen the connection between doctoral education, research, and applied organizational practice.   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Supervisory Responsibilities ·         No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ·         Doctoral degree in Organizational Behavior Management, Behavior Analysis, Organizational Behavior, Applied Behavioral Science, or a closely related field. ·         Demonstrated expertise in research methodology, including single-subject and group experimental designs. ·         Demonstrated expertise in scientific and scholarly writing and APA style. ·         Advanced expertise in conducting systematic literature reviews, including familiarity with established methodologies such as PRISMA. ·         Experience advising, mentoring, teaching, or otherwise supporting graduate or doctoral students. ·         Demonstrated scholarly or professional engagement in areas related to business, leadership, organizational behavior management, organizational behavior science, or applied behavioral science. ·         Professional experience in business, industry, consulting, research, or applied organizational settings. ·         Strong written, oral, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. ·         Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities independently and collaboratively.   Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience teaching at the doctoral level. ·         Experience serving as a dissertation chair or committee member. ·         Experience supporting or navigating Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes. ·         Experience with data visualization and statistical software, such as GraphPad Prism, or comparable platforms. ·         Demonstrated record of publications, presentations, or other scholarly dissemination. ·         Experience working across multiple organizational or industry settings, such as healthcare, manufacturing, energy, safety, or other complex environments. ·         Experience developing partnerships with business, industry, community, or professional organizations. ·         Experience supporting doctoral program development, academic administration, or continuous program improvement.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $70,000–$92,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Registrar--Reporting-and-Data-Analytics_JREQ-002668": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar, Reporting and Data Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Job Summary Reporting to the Registrar, the Associate Registrar provides business analysis and develops data reports for the Office of the Registrar. This position also manages student enrollment and degree verification reporting to the National Student Clearinghouse, ensuring compliance with regulatory reporting requirements. Additional responsibilities include overseeing the transcript Evaluation process, and supporting the maintenance of the degree audit system and academic plans for each academic year.   Key Outcomes 50% of Time:  Develop and maintain reports that support the operations of the Office of the Registrar. ●        Gather, document, and analyze business needs and reporting requirements for the Office of the Registrar, developing new reports to support the day-to-day operations of the office. ●        Develop, maintain, and optimize reports using Workday Student reporting tools to support academic and administrative departments, as well as third-party requests and federal and state regulatory requirements. ●        Collaborate with academic and administrative offices to identify reporting needs, define requirements, and develop solutions that provide accurate and actionable information. ●        Work proactively with internal and external stakeholders to revise and deliver accurate, user-friendly institutional reports that meet operational and regulatory needs. ●        Interpret and evaluate historical data to ensure operation-critical reports are current, accurate, consistent, and available when needed. ●        Perform data validation and quality checks to identify discrepancies, investigate data issues, and ensure the accuracy and integrity of information used for reporting and decision-making. ●        Analyze existing reports and reporting processes to identify opportunities for increased efficiency, automation, and improved data quality. ●        Maintain documentation for reports, including business requirements, data sources, report logic, definitions, and standard procedures to support consistency and knowledge transfer. ●        Serve as a subject matter resource for Registrar's Office reporting and assist faculty and staff in understanding and appropriately using Registrar-related data and reports. ●        Collaborate with Information Technology and other campus partners to troubleshoot reporting issues, identify system limitations, and develop solutions to meet business requirements. ●        Monitor changes to Workday Student functionality and institutional reporting requirements and assess their potential impact on existing reports and Registrar's Office operations. ●        Provide ad hoc data analysis and reporting to support operational needs, institutional initiatives, audits, and decision-making.   30% of Time:  Generate enrollment files for submission to the National Clearinghouse (NSC). ●        Understand NSC/NSLDS regulatory and reporting requirements. ●        Responsible for submitting enrollment and graduate files on a regular schedule throughout the academic year. ●        Analyze and communicate with auditors and Registrar to quickly resolve errors that may arise during end-of-term processing. ●        Archive and track submitted reports as required by federal and state regulations.   20 % of Time:  Maintain complete and accurate documentation of technical processes used in or relevant to the Office of the Registrar. ●        Collaborate with the team to develop and maintain standard operating procedure documentation (SOPs) to ensure best practices are documented accurately on time. ●        Provide first-level customer support and troubleshoot system issues related to reporting practices. ●        Serve as liaison between the Office of the Registrar and Information Technology. ●        Support the Provost’s Office on special projects, including but not limited to preparing timely reports for Academic Review, communicating with the necessary parties in advance, holding the Academic Review sessions over the course of the academic year, sending official letters to students, and following up on particular student cases with deans. ●        Other duties as assigned.   Core Competencies   Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills   has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service The employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members   Education & Experience ●      Bachelor’s degree in Management Information Systems or related field or equivalent experience.  ●      Minimum of five years of experience in business analysis or a related field. Knowledge of higher education institutional data is preferred. ●      Minimum of three years of experience with Workday Student reporting or higher education student information systems (SIS), with experience working in a Registrar’s Office or similar academic administrative environment preferred.   Skills & Abilities ●      Sound understanding of FERPA and National Student Clearinghouse compliance. ●      Exceptional analytical and conceptual thinking skills. ●      Strong customer service skills. ●      Sound decision-making ability to determine acceptable solutions. ●      Strong written and oral communication skills. ●      Ability to work independently and in a team environment. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $72,500–$85,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Provost---Chief-Academic-Officer_JREQ-002654": {
      "title": "Provost & Chief Academic Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Endicott College seeks an accomplished, forward-thinking Provost and Chief Academic Officer to guide its academic strategy during a period of sustained institutional growth and innovation. Known for its required three-internship model, The Endicott Experiential Edge , the College serves approximately 3,100 traditional undergraduate students, 300 adult undergraduate students, and 1,500 graduate students across its schools and academic programs. Supported by more than $80 million in academic infrastructure investments and $20 million in campus enhancements supporting the student experience since 2019, Endicott offers a strong foundation for continued academic advancement. The next Provost will help shape the future of teaching and learning by expanding high-demand undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs; supporting faculty scholarship; strengthening interdisciplinary pathways; and preparing the College to respond thoughtfully and strategically to an increasingly AI-driven world. Endicott is a relational, close-knit global community that values accessibility, collaboration, and visible leadership. The successful candidate will be an approachable, accessible, and engaged leader who builds meaningful relationships across the College and embraces a “management by walking around” philosophy. The Provost will work closely with faculty leadership and the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA), fostering open communication, meaningful collaboration, and a strong commitment to shared governance. Reporting directly to the President and as a key member of the President’s Cabinet and the College’s chief academic officer, the Provost will have a significant opportunity to influence Endicott’s academic direction. The role calls for an agile and entrepreneurial leader who can bridge traditional academic affairs silos, elevate research and scholarship, and pursue strategic growth while preserving the mentor-rich, student-centered culture that defines the Endicott experience. Located just 20 miles north of Boston on a picturesque 235-acre oceanfront campus, Endicott offers its next Provost the opportunity to join a vibrant and highly collaborative community. For an inspiring academic leader who deeply respects the College’s history and traditions while eagerly embracing its future, the Endicott Provostship presents an extraordinary opportunity to make a meaningful and lasting impact. Please view the full Provost profile here . To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Responsibilities The Provost will lead Endicott’s academic enterprise, strengthen its academic profile and operational capacity, expand institutional partnerships, and position the College for continued innovation and sustainable growth. 40%: Academic Strategy, Leadership, and Institutional Planning Develop and advance a comprehensive academic vision aligned with the College’s mission and strategic priorities. Lead academic planning across undergraduate, graduate, professional, and doctoral programs. Provide effective leadership, support, and accountability for Academic Deans and academic administrative leaders. Evaluate and evolve the academic portfolio in response to student needs, market trends, institutional priorities, and emerging opportunities. Partner with senior leadership to advance enrollment strategy, financial sustainability, and institutional growth. Ensure that academic programs maintain high standards of quality, relevance, and student success. Guide the evolution of academic programs and signature internship pathways in response to emerging technologies, while protecting academic integrity. Strengthen connections among undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. 35%: Faculty Excellence, Academic Quality, and Shared Governance Foster a culture of teaching excellence, scholarship, innovation, and continuous improvement among faculty. Serve as the College’s senior academic leader. Develop and maintain effective partnerships across the campus community, including ECFA, adjunct faculty, and academic affairs staff, advance academic priorities, and support a positive campus culture. Support effective faculty recruitment, retention, development, promotion, and recognition practices. Oversee academic policies, accreditation expectations, assessment practices, and academic integrity. Promote a collaborative environment grounded in transparency, communication, and a belief that all members of the Endicott community have an equal voice. Collaborate with administrative leaders to streamline academic workflows and operations (such as advising and administrative systems).  25%: Executive Leadership, Collaboration, and External Engagement Serve as the President’s primary advisor on academic matters and a key member of the President’s Cabinet. Collaborate equally with the President’s Cabinet across the College to align academic priorities with institutional goals. Represent Endicott’s academic mission with trustees, accrediting organizations, industry partners, donors, and external stakeholders. Champion Endicott’s distinctive experiential learning model, ensuring The Endicott Experiential Edge remains central to the academic experience. Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events in each division of the college. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Establish and maintain a robust, interactive, and transparent working relationship with the President’s Cabinet. Other duties as assigned Supervisory Responsibilities Associate Provost, Academic Affairs (overseeing academic operations, experiential learning integration, honors programs, and key academic events). Academic Deans (Undergraduate Schools, including Business, Education, Nursing & Health Sciences, Science & Technology, Social Sciences/Humanities/Communication, Sport Science, and Visual & Performing Arts).   Office Staff : Executive Assistant / Administrative Assistant  Core Competencies Strategic and Entrepreneurial Leadership :  Identifies emerging higher education trends, balances academic tradition with market agility, and translates big-picture vision into achievable operational outcomes. Collaborative Governance and Relationship Building :  Engages authentically with faculty, staff, students, and trustees; navigates complex organizational dynamics with transparency, empathy, and respect. Experiential Education Philosophy :  Possesses a deep, unwavering commitment to applied learning, profession-readiness, and student-centered outcomes. Financial and Data Literacy :  Uses quantitative and qualitative data to guide resource allocation, assess program viability, and manage complex divisional budgets effectively. Decisive and Steady Management :  Navigates ambiguity and complex institutional challenges with clear judgment, steady communication, and personal integrity. Qualifications & Skills An earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution is required. A distinguished record of teaching, scholarship or creative activity, and service appropriate for appointment as a full professor or equivalent academic standing is required. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible leadership experience in higher education administration. Demonstrated experience leading academic organizations, including supervising academic leaders, allocating resources strategically, and driving data-driven decisions using modern administrative systems (familiarity with or utilization of Workday preferred).  Experience developing, evaluating, and evolving academic programs in response to student needs, institutional goals, market trends, and emerging opportunities across undergraduate, graduate, professional, online, and hybrid learning environments. Demonstrated ability to foster strong relationships and work collaboratively with faculty, staff, executive leaders, staff, executive leaders, academic leaders, and campus stakeholders. Experience advancing partnerships with external organizations, including industry, community, alumni, and philanthropic partners, to support academic opportunities and institutional goals. Demonstrated ability to anticipate and navigate macro-level trends and disruptive forces in higher education, leveraging innovative approaches to adapt academic structures and program offerings for future growth.  Strong understanding of accreditation, assessment, academic quality standards, and continuous improvement practices. Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build trust, inspire confidence, and effectively engage diverse internal and external audiences. Demonstrated commitment to student success, experiential learning, and preparing graduates for professional and lifelong achievement. Demonstrated experience working collaboratively with faculty leadership, executive leadership, trustees.  Experience fostering productive relationships with faculty unions or collective bargaining units. Preferred Attributes The ideal candidate will demonstrate: A deep commitment to Endicott’s distinctive identity , including its integration of the liberal arts, professional preparation, and experiential learning. A strong academic foundation and meaningful classroom teaching experience , providing firsthand knowledge of pedagogy, student engagement, scholarship, and faculty responsibilities. An accessible and visible leadership style , with an authentic interest in participating in the life of the campus community. Emotional intelligence and thoughtful self-regulation , including the patience to listen, understand the institutional culture and history before initiating significant change. A collaborative and service-oriented leadership approach , encouraging open dialogue across faculty, staff, students, and administration while working constructively within collective bargaining structures. Intellectual curiosity , with genuine appreciation for a wide range of academic disciplines and the value of interdisciplinary collaboration. Forward-thinking adaptability in technology , recognizing the potential of emerging tools to strengthen teaching, learning, and career preparation while preserving meaningful human connection. A holistic commitment to the student experience , supporting academic achievement, student well-being, personal responsibility, and coordinated advising. Strategic ambition for institutional growth , with an interest in elevating Endicott’s regional and national profile, expanding its geographic reach, and strengthening pathways among undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. Approachability, warmth, and authentic care for others , reinforcing Endicott’s relational culture and ensuring that people across roles and areas of the College feel seen, respected, and valued. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $285,000–$300,000 . Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Review of applications for the Provost of Endicott College will begin immediately and continue until October 24, 2026. To assure full consideration, applications should be received by October 24, 2026 at 1 p.m. EDT, and must include: • A letter of interest addressing the strategic objectives and qualifications identified in this profile; • A current curriculum vitae; and • The contact information (email and phone) for five professional references, including their relationship to the candidate. The Search Committee will not reach out until the candidate is notified."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Business-Analyst_JREQ-002652": {
      "title": "Business Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Business Analyst in the Information Technology department, reporting to the Director of Enterprise Applications, is responsible for the coordination, management, testing and development of ancillary applications and secondary support of the College's Enterprise Applications. The IT Business Analyst will be working with the other IT Business Analysts and Enterprise Applications developers to gather requirements, manage projects, coordinate testing, and validate data.  The IT Business Analyst will work with the College’s Functional Areas to recommend and support business process needs and improvements. This role is full-time, and will be required to be on campus a minimum of 3 days a week with the opportunity to work remotely up to 2 days a week, as agreed upon with the Reporting Manager. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   *** To be considered for this role, a cover letter is required. In the cover letter, please articulate why you want to be considered for the role, and why working at Endicott College is interesting to you.*** Key Responsibilities   60% of Time: Workday ERP and SIS Support ●     Assist in managing Workday-related projects and enhancement request. ●     Support configuration of Workday business processes, integrations, condition rules, and validation criteria. ●     Troubleshoots and resolves complex development, testing, and production issues. ●     Create and maintain documentation for requirements gathering, business processes, integrations, procedures, and system configuration. 20% of Time: Project Management ·         Collect, analyze, and translate business requirements into user stories, workflows, business process logic, process maps, wireframes, specifications, and acceptance criteria. ·         Monitor deliverables and ensure timely completion of projects through developing project plans and monitoring performance. ·         Ensure solutions meet business needs and requirements. ·         Adhere to the College's information security policies and follow information security procedures.  ·         Consult with the College's information security staff for guidance on best practices. 10% of Time: Support Operations ·         Daily Ticket Triage: Monitor the Freshservice ticketing queue daily, conducting initial triage, troubleshooting, and independent research to resolve technical and operational issues prior to escalation where appropriate. 10% of Time: Planning and Partnership ·         Engage with internal stakeholders to determine a strategy and vision for software applications, including business needs and requirements. ·         Serve as a liaison between stakeholders and users, building strong relationships and becoming a trusted partner and subject matter expert. ·         Create and maintain business relationships with respective stakeholders on campus, and support their work and functional needs with relevant expertise.   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Other Duties ·         Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Enterprise Applications. Works under general supervision   Supervisory Responsibilities None   Core Competencies   Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·         Bachelor's degree in related field or equivalent work experience ·         3+ years of related experience ·         Ability to use Excel and other tools to manipulate data ·         Experience with tools like Jira, Confluence, MS Project, LucidChart ·         Demonstrates strong communication and writing skills for both technical and non-technical audiences ·         Excellent problem-solving skills ·         Excellent time management and prioritization skills ·         Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities and meet negotiated timelines with high quality deliverables Preferred Experience in higher education Workday Experience   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $75,000–$85,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  Month, Year September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Grounds-Equipment-Operator_JREQ-002650": {
      "title": "Grounds Equipment Operator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Grounds/Equipment Operator is responsible for maintaining Endicott College's buildings, grounds, and equipment. This role performs a variety of tasks, including landscaping, snow removal, assisting with event setup and breakdown, handling routine maintenance and minor repairs, and completing work orders. The position contributes to a functional, safe, and welcoming campus environment. Flexibility, problem-solving skills, and a collaborative approach are essential to success in this role. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Performs grounds maintenance tasks, including planting trees and shrubs, mowing lawns, trimming hedges, and collecting leaves to keep the campus looking its best. Clears snow and ice from parking lots, walkways, and other areas to keep pathways safe and accessible. Assists with setup, breakdown, and cleanup for events and functions, ensuring timely and efficient service. General laborer work includes moving and arranging furniture, equipment, and supplies as needed, in accordance with safety guidelines. Completes minor repairs and maintenance projects as assigned or in response to work orders. Troubleshoots and performs minor repairs on equipment to keep it operating properly. Picks up trash and disposes of waste daily to keep the environment clean and safe. Performs miscellaneous tasks and assignments as directed to support departmental operations. Participates in the on-call rotation policy to address urgent needs and emergencies. Performs other duties as needed to support department and campus goals. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Grounds. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills A minimum of two years of experience in facilities operations, grounds maintenance, or general repair work, preferably in a college or institutional environment. Proven reliability, a strong work ethic, and a consistent record of meeting job commitments and deadlines. Demonstrated ability to provide responsive, professional customer service while maintaining a positive, helpful attitude during interactions with students, staff, and visitors. Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in performing tasks and completing documentation. Strong collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively as part of a team while remaining accountable for individual performance. Ability to work overtime or flexible hours in response to events or emergency situations. Practical skills and knowledge to perform assigned tasks effectively. Adaptability and a positive approach to handling varied responsibilities. A minimum of a High School diploma or equivalent. Ability to climb ladders, lift up to 50 lbs., and perform physically demanding tasks. Knowledge of day-to-day operations in a college environment. Must provide proof of a valid Mass. driver's license and a current DOT medical form annually. Ability to obtain and maintain a valid Department of Public Safety Hoisting License. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $22.60–$25.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Women-s-Tennis-Coach_JREQ-002644": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Coach, Women’s Tennis, Seasonal reporting to the Head Women’s Tennis Coach within the Department of Athletics, provides part-time, seasonal support for the College’s NCAA Division III women’s tennis program. The position assists the Head Coach with practices, match preparation, student-athlete instruction and development, recruiting, conditioning, and other team-related activities. The Assistant Coach, Women’s Tennis, Seasonal works collaboratively with the Head Coach to provide a positive, competitive, and supportive experience for student-athletes while helping to maintain a program that reflects the mission and values of Endicott College and the Department of Athletics. This position is expected to work primarily during scheduled practices, competitions, recruiting activities, and other program-related activities as assigned by the Head Coach. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. Key Responsibilities Coaching and Practice Support (40%) Assist the Head Coach with the planning and implementation of scheduled team practices. Provide tennis instruction and individual or small-group coaching to student-athletes. Assist with drills, skill development, match preparation, and team activities. Provide constructive feedback and instruction to student-athletes in support of their athletic development. Help promote a positive team environment focused on sportsmanship, accountability, teamwork, and personal growth. When requested and appropriate, assist with or take responsibility for a scheduled practice in the absence of the Head Coach. Match and Competition Support (40%) Assist the Head Coach with preparation for scheduled matches and competitions. Assist with match-day organization, warm-ups, team preparation, and student-athlete support. Provide coaching and instruction during competitions as directed by the Head Coach. Assist with scouting and preparation for opponents. When requested and appropriate, assist with a match in the absence of the Head Coach. Recruiting and Student-Athlete Development (5%) Assist the Head Coach with recruiting activities and the identification of prospective student-athletes. Support recruiting communications, campus visits, and recruiting events as requested. Assist the Head Coach in providing appropriate support and mentorship to student-athletes. Serve as a positive role model for student-athletes and contribute to their overall development. Follow all applicable NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics policies related to recruiting and student-athlete contact. Program and Team Support (10%) Assist with team travel and transportation as assigned and as scheduling permits. Assist with equipment, supplies, uniforms, and other team needs. Help maintain organized and appropriate tennis equipment and practice areas. Assist with basic program-related administrative tasks as requested by the Head Coach. Represent Endicott College and the Department of Athletics in a professional manner at practices, competitions, recruiting events, and other assigned activities. Community Engagement (5%) Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned. Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Women’s Tennis Coach. Works under the general direction of the Head Coach and receives regular direction regarding coaching, recruiting, practices, competitions, and other assigned program responsibilities. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required. Knowledge of tennis instruction, training, competition, and student-athlete development. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to effectively work with college-age student-athletes. Ability to work collaboratively with the Head Coach and members of the Department of Athletics. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends consistent with the team’s practice and competition schedule. Ability to travel occasionally with the team, as assigned and as scheduling permits. Ability to comply with NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics rules, policies, and procedures. Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications Previous collegiate tennis coaching experience. Collegiate tennis playing experience. Experience working with student-athletes in a coaching, mentoring, or instructional capacity. Experience with recruiting prospective student-athletes. Knowledge of NCAA Division III athletics. Relevant tennis coaching certifications or professional development. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay for this position is $2,000 per season. This pay reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Carpentry-Supervisor_JREQ-002629": {
      "title": "Carpentry Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Reporting to the Associate Vice Presidents of Facilities Operations, the Supervisor of Carpentry is a working supervisor responsible for repairs, preventive maintenance, work orders, and renovations. You will lead a skilled in-house team of carpenters and a locksmith, and coordinate with other departments to ensure that all college-owned historic and modern facilities are in good repair, remain safe, sustainable, and fully operational. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Supervise and lead the daily operations of the carpentry shop, including assigning work, scheduling staff, and ensuring quality workmanship. Maintain and repair campus facilities by overseeing and performing skilled carpentry work for academic, residential, and administrative buildings. Plan and coordinate projects, including estimating labor and materials, prioritizing work orders, and collaborating with other Facilities Management administration, trades and campus departments. Ensure a safe work environment by enforcing OSHA regulations, College safety policies, and applicable building codes. Manage shop operations, including inventory, tools, equipment, and maintenance records. Provide excellent customer service by promptly responding to maintenance requests and communicating effectively with faculty, staff, students, and contractors. Obtain quotes, coordinate with, and oversee outside contractors as necessary. Support emergency response and campus operations, including after-hours emergencies, severe weather, snow removal, and special projects. Participates in the on-call policy. Performs other duties as needed to meet the needs and goals of the department and College. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and all other hands-on-deck gatherings. Show spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Vice President of Facilities Operations Supervisory Responsibilities Supervisory responsibilities – 3 Carpenters and a Locksmith Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Resourceful: a problem solver who can make informed decisions and can juggle multiple projects. Adaptability: exhibit a willingness to implement innovative ideas while accommodating change during fluid and evolving circumstances. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills High School Diploma or equivalent. Unrestricted Construction Supervisor License (CSL). OSHA 10 or 30 Hours certifications. Typically 8-10 or more years of progressively responsible experience in commercial, institutional, or facilities carpentry. Demonstrated knowledge of building construction methods, finish carpentry, cabinetry, framing, doors, drywall, hardware, and related building systems. Ability to read and interpret blueprints, specifications, and construction documents. Experience estimating materials, labor, and project costs. Proficiency using standard carpentry tools and woodworking equipment. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Must be computer literate and familiar with a computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Must provide proof of valid Mass driver's license and DOT medical form annually. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $37 - $50.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Per-Diem-Athletic-Trainers_JREQ-002298": {
      "title": "Per Diem Athletic Trainers",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Per Diem Athletic Trainer in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Head Athletic Trainer, is responsible for providing temporary, on-site coverage for athletics events (in-season practices and contests, non-traditional contests, post-season contests, camps and skills clinics) for all varsity or club teams at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Duties can include care and prevention of athletic injuries, wellness promotion, examination, assessment, diagnosis, immediate care, emergency care, therapeutic intervention, healthcare organization, administration and professional responsibility for all varsity and club student-athletes and on-site practice/contest coverage. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities  Provide Athletic Training Services (70%)  o Provide on-site athletic training services for practices and athletic contests hosted by Endicott College.  o Comply with all NCAA, Conference affiliated, athletic department, industry, and institutional guidelines, recommendations, and regulations.  o The employee will be a person of integrity with high ethical standards that adheres to the NATA Code of Ethics and institutional guidelines. Adheres to the state practice act, all NATA and NCAA best practices, and standing orders specified by the team physician.  o Provides counseling and education of student-athletes within the scope of practice.  Evaluate Athletic Injuries and Illnesses (20%)  o Evaluate athletic injuries and illness sustained by a varsity or club student-athlete and refer to other health care professionals as necessary.  o Provide urgent and emergent care as needed by the situation following NATA and NCAA best practices.  o Provide treatment and rehabilitation exercises for athletic injuries or illnesses as needed    Administrative Duties (10%)  o Document all injuries and treatments provided and communicate injuries with full time Athletic Training staff  o Maintain cleanliness and safety of the equipment in the Athletic Training clinic(s)  o Works with the coaching staff and other Athletic Department personnel to ensure the safety of all facilities, environments, and equipment used for intercollegiate athletics  Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Athletic Trainer Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills   ● Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training  ● Valid national certification from the BOC  ● Valid CPR/AED Certification  ● Valid Massachusetts State licensure through the Board of Allied Health Professionals  ● Demonstrated ability to interact effectively with college-age students  ● Strong verbal and written communication skills  ● Possesses the ability to lift heavy objects, stand for long periods, work in various environmental conditions  ● Assist injured individuals on/off playing surfaces  ● Coverage can include availability of mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays  ● Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters    Preferred Qualifications N/A  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $53.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version: December 2025"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--School-of-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences_JREQ-002613": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs is a member of the leadership team for the School of Nursing. Under the direction of the Dean and in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Undergraduate programs is responsible for leadership and oversight of the development, implementation, and evaluation of outstanding, innovative academic programs in the School of Nursing. This position assumes responsibility for the accreditation, curriculum development, and evaluation and assessment of all program outcomes .  The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs will provide leadership and direction to faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, help to meet expected program outcomes, as well as align with the Endicott College mission to provide students with meaningful experiential learning. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities  Lead the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (40%) Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) Leads the SON in assessment and evaluation of all program outcomes. Develops, oversees, and implements the evaluation process of all programs, including survey development, refinement, and analysis of outcomes. Works with the Dean to develop and implement the systematic plan of evaluation and reporting to accreditation agencies. Ensure a high-quality graduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes that features meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies in line with the mission of the School of Nursing and the college. (40%) Ensure licensure and certification success through oversight, implementation, and effective use of programs (Fitzgerald Course). Collaborate with Program Chairs regarding curricular needs for adjunct laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointing, orienting, and mentoring of faculty members while also creating an atmosphere of inclusivity and community within the SON. Oversee regular performance evaluations of faculty and professional staff to ensure continuous improvement. Oversee direct reports and promote a positive and inclusive work environment that supports the professional growth of staff while fostering a commitment to academic innovation and excellence. Assist the Dean in development and management of the operating and capital budgets. Represent the SON in the community through participation in scholarship, service, and professional development activities that promote the school. (20%) Support Admission and Recruiting events – especially at the graduate level, which requires the Associate Dean to work very closely with the Admission/Recruiting and Marketing/Communications Department (website design) and program chairs to establish and implement effective recruiting measures for graduate programs. Attain revenue targets for the graduate programs. Advises students based on the needs of the school. Teaches 2 courses/year based on the needs of the school. Other duties as assigned Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or related field; experience with a professional accreditation; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students); Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA; Strong computer experience, which must include the ability to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000-$165,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit your resume/CV and a cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--Undergrad-Nursing-Programs_JREQ-002612-1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Undergrad Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs serves as a member of the School of Nursing leadership team. Reporting to the Dean and working in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Nursing Programs and the Associate Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, this position provides leadership and oversight for the development, implementation, and evaluation of innovative, high-quality undergraduate academic programs within the School of Nursing. The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs supports the advancement of academic excellence by guiding faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, support the achievement of expected program outcomes, and align with the Endicott College mission of providing meaningful experiential learning opportunities. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Ensure a high-quality undergraduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes, supported by meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies that align with the mission of the School of Nursing and the College. (25%) Monitor NCLEX pass rates at or above the School of Nursing’s expected level of achievement, while meeting accreditation benchmarks and state and national pass rate expectations. Support licensure success through the oversight, implementation, and effective use of student success and assessment resources, including ATI. Collaborate with undergraduate Program Chairs to identify curricular needs related to adjunct, laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointment, orientation, and mentoring of faculty members while fostering a culture of inclusivity, collegiality, and community within the School of Nursing. Participate in hiring faculty for undergraduates and oversee their continued professional growth. Supervise direct reports and promote a positive, inclusive work environment that supports professional growth, academic innovation, and excellence. Assist the Dean with the development and management of operating and capital budgets. Ensure a positive and supportive student experience through direct oversight of student issues across all undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Serve as the primary point of contact for undergraduate student issues in collaboration with Program Chairs, full-time faculty, academic advisors, and appropriate college departments, including Student Success, Housing, Health Services, Career Services, International Education, Community Service, the Chaplain’s Office, Athletics, the Registrar, Financial Aid, and Admissions. Provide leadership and support related to student progression, academic concerns, retention, professionalism, and overall student success across the undergraduate nursing programs. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and college departments to address student needs in a timely, fair, consistent, and student-centered manner. Provide leadership and oversight for simulation centers and laboratories, clinical education, and internship experiences within the undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Collaborate with the Director of Simulation and Labs and the Director of the Clinical Placement Office to ensure that: Experiential learning opportunities are meaningful, well-coordinated, and aligned with program outcomes. Clinical, simulation-based, and internship experiences strengthen students’ clinical judgment, professional development, and readiness for nursing practice. Faculty, clinical partners, and professional staff collaborate effectively to promote consistency, quality, and continuous improvement across experiential learning settings. Required accreditation processes, standards, and documentation are consistently followed, maintained, and evaluated in these areas Support School of Nursing operations, student advising, recruitment, and professional engagement through service to the school, college, and broader community. (15%) Support Admission and Recruiting events Advise students based on the needs of the school. Support the Academic Coordinator with the Course of Study and oversee student registration and scheduling concerns. Assist the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (10%) MA Board of Registration in Nursing (MABORN) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE)  Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or MSN with 5 years' experience in a related field; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate level; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students);  Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA;  Strong computer experience, which must include abilities to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000–$165,000 Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit a resume/CV and cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Cummings-Center-for-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences/Assistant-Professor--Doctor-of-Nursing-Practice--DNP-_JREQ-002184-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing teaches courses for the Graduate Nursing Program. They also advise students, participate in accreditation processes; engage in professional scholarship or development, assist in the development of internship relationships and student opportunities, and participate in school and college-wide service. They will teach courses and advise students for two semesters.   This position is covered by the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College. ECFA is a faculty union organized under the NEA (National Education Association) and provides structure and support for all full-time faculty at Endicott College.  The Cummings School of Nursing and Health Sciences is seeking a dynamic, full-time DNP Faculty member passionate about shaping the next generation of healthcare executives and clinical experts. As a vital educator in our growing Doctor of Nursing Practice program, you will leverage your expertise in healthcare leadership and clinical inquiry to teach advanced courses in both quantitative and qualitative methodologies. If you are ready to inspire doctoral students and drive innovation in healthcare delivery, this is your opportunity to make a lasting institutional impact. In this pivotal role, you will directly influence patient outcomes by championing Evidence-Based Practice (EBP) and Quality Improvement (QI) initiatives within our curriculum. You will have the opportunity to mentor, advise, and guide students through their culminating DNP Scholarly Practice Projects, translating evidence based practice into real-world clinical solutions. If you hold a Doctor of Nursing Practice degree, possess a strong background in organizational leadership, and thrive in a collaborative academic environment, apply today to join our forward-thinking nursing faculty. This is a year round position. Responsibilities include:  Teach 24 credits per academic year -- 12 credits in both the fall and spring semesters (4 lecture courses each semester, or equivalent). Advise up to 25 students.  Attend department, school, and college meetings.  Participate in accreditation processes.  Engage in professional development, scholarship, research, and/or publishing.  Assist in curriculum development.   Participate in department, school, and college service.  Maintain and post regular office hours.   Perform other duties as required and as outlined in the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College.  Participate in course development and implementation.  Evaluate teaching/learning activities  Participate in governance, including the School of Nursing All School Committee and other committees as appointed   Requirement / Qualifications A doctorate in Nursing or a related field is required Must have or be eligible for RN licensure in Massachusetts Hold at least one graduate degree in nursing in the area of specialization required for the faculty appointment 3-5 years of experience in the related field of nursing Prior teaching experience in a nursing program is desired, and required at the Associate Professor Level Demonstrated ability to relate to a diverse student body Commitment to scholarship appropriate to the rank Demonstrate excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the compensation for this faculty position is established through the College’s contractual salary structure. Pay rates are set for each faculty rank and appointment type. This position carries a fixed annual salary of $98,602.12 (Assistant Professor) or $115,161.61 (Associate Professor) for a 12-month appointment. This amount represents base salary only and does not include benefits or other forms of compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director--Criminal-Justice-Graduate-Program_JREQ-002538": {
      "title": "Director, Criminal Justice Graduate Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Director of the Criminal Justice (CJ) Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. The Director is responsible for leading the strategic launch, growth, and daily operations of a newly designed CJ Graduate Program, which features a soft launch in Spring 2027 and full implementation in Fall 2027. This role includes managing curriculum development, supervising full and part-time faculty, overseeing program evaluation/accreditation, and driving student enrollment and retention. This is an in-person, on-campus position. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Dedicated to Student Success (30%) Directs graduate academic advising, guiding students from admission through progression and successful completion of their degree. Implements a proactive advising model, including onboarding new advisees prior to program entry and conducting regular progress checks. Collaborates with the Associate Dean to identify, support, and coach at-risk students to maximize retention. Maintains high-quality advising standards to ensure timely student progress through coursework and career alignment. Contributes to the overall success of the CJ graduate program (30%) Leads the successful implementation and execution of the new CJ graduate program’s soft launch (Spring 2027) and full launch (Fall 2027) in coordination with the Associate Dean. Partners closely with the Homeland Security Graduate Program Director to integrate existing HLS concentration courses into the CJ curriculum and provide seamless cross-program pathways for students. Collaborates with the Director of the Cybercrime Forensics Lab to coordinate the cybersecurity concentration, including lab exercises, simulations, and hands-on training. Drives recruitment, enrollment growth, and student retention initiatives to sustain an 80%+ retention and graduation rate. Manages ongoing program assessment, continuous improvement, and accreditation efforts at the course, program, and school levels. Contributes to the College community through service on school-wide and institutional committees. Teaches and develops courses in CJ/HLS graduate programs (20%) Teaches 2 graduate-level courses per year across the CJ and HLS programs. Demonstrates excellence in teaching through strong student evaluations and the utilization of diverse, effective assessment strategies. Develops cutting-edge course content and materials aligned with current industry trends, program needs, and School standards. Supervises, trains, and evaluates adjunct faculty (10%) Collaborates with the Associate Dean to recruit, hire, train, and evaluate part-time adjunct faculty within the CJ graduate program. Ensures all adjunct faculty align their courses with Canvas LMS standards and School pedagogical benchmarks. Reviews student course evaluations annually with faculty to implement data-driven pedagogical adjustments. Increases Endicott’s reputation in the field of CJ graduate education (10%) Maintains an active track record of scholarship and research in criminal justice or a related field. Represents the College and its graduate programs through the presentation of academic scholarship at national and state conferences, seminars, or through peer-reviewed publications. Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Reporting Structure The Director of the Criminal Justice Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. Supervisory Responsibilities Collaborates with the Associate Dean to hire, supervise, train, and evaluate 100% of part-time graduate adjunct professors. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Ph.D. or terminal degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related field highly preferred ; a Master’s degree or JD with significant academic leadership and operational experience considered. Documented record of academic scholarship and active participation in national or regional professional organizations. Demonstrated excellence in graduate-level teaching, including experience with online, lab-based, or hybrid simulation models. Strong collaborative skills with a proven ability to work across departments (e.g., working alongside Homeland Security or Cybersecurity disciplines). Commitment to inclusive education, social justice, and developing cultural competencies among a diverse, non-traditional, and adult student population. Excellent organizational and technical proficiency, including experience with Canvas LMS, MS Office, and Google Workspace. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $94,000 .00   and $115,000.00. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  July 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Roller-Hockey--Seasonal-_JREQ-002134-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Roller Hockey (Seasonal)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-22\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Roller Hockey Coach in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Associate Director of Athletics collaborates with the athletics department advisor and team leaders to set goals, develop budgets, evaluate organizational needs, problem-solve, and serve as a liaison with other college departments essential to program implementation and success.This is a part-time, seasonal position and is a fantastic opportunity to work with a thriving collegiate club to play a key role in the clubs continued development and success. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities The Assistant Coach will be inheriting a group of highly talented and motivated men that have continued to compete at Nationals every year. Coaching Duties (80%) Providing instruction, mentoring and guidance to student athletes to allow them to develop their athletic skills and abilities to maximum potential. Evaluating athletic ability and performance. Assuring that equipment and practice plans are prepared in advance of practice sessions. Maintaining positive and professional relations with students, athletes, and alumni Ability to teach safe and proper technique to beginning level players while challenging and integrating the skills of higher-level players Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned Program Administrative Support (20%) Coordinate scheduling, meals, transportation, etc for all team trips in conjunction with the head coach Track team expenses and process invoices Please note: Under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), position descriptions should focus on essential functions , those that, if removed, would fundamentally change the job. Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Director, Athletics. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Minimum education or training needed to be considered for the role At least one year of relevant experience Specific skills or qualifications necessary to be successful If applicable, note any travel, evening, or weekend requirements If the role involves working with sensitive information, include: “Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters” In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $2,000–$2,500 per season. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Architectural---Design-Studies_JREQ-002418": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Architectural + Design Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-20\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Visual + Performing Arts, Department of Architectural + Design Studies is currently seeking individuals to teach undergraduate and graduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture courses for the 2026-2027 academic calendar year. We are seeking multiple adjunct instructors for foundational architectural studies courses and major-specific courses for the following Undergraduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture Majors : Architectural Sketching (4-hour studio) Building Information Modeling (REVIT and RHINO) (4-hour studio) Interior Hospitality Studio (6-hour studio) Graduate Interior Architecture: Graduate Design Theory All courses are in-person unless noted otherwise. Each lecture course meets as indicated above. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $4,700-$4,800 per course. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks through the entire semester. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s  Faculty Handbook . Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Bartender_JREQ-002335-1": {
      "title": "Bartender",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-07\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Misselwood at Endicott College is a breathtaking oceanfront estate with historic charm, offering panoramic views and serving as the premier location for world-class events in Beverly, MA. We are seeking bartenders to work our weddings and events during the season.  This role requires work on weekends. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities     ·        Responsibly serve alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages to event guest ·        Accurately check IDs ·        Responsible for monetary transactions while operating the cash register ·        Perform the set up and break down of the bar ·        Cleaning and ensuring dish machine is turned off at the end of the night ·        Responsible for counting empty beer bottles and soda bottles for event inventory sheet ·        Responsible for refilling the juice, sodas, beer and wine behind the bar for events ·        Restocking and keeping track of inventory needs ·        Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Event Operations. During events, will take direction from head bartender     Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities   Core Competencies     Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·        18 years or older ·        ServeSafe or TIPS certified required ·        Must be able to work late hours ·        Must be able to work weekends and holidays ·        Required to stand for long periods of time ·        Must be able to lift up to 35 pounds ·        Excellent communication and customer service skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay for this position is $6.75 per hour PLUS tips. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  March 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Graduate-School-of-Education_JREQ-002332": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Graduate School of Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-12\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Education is currently seeking individuals to teach the following content in the Fall semester, with classes starting on September 1, 2026 and ending on November 23, 2026: School Counseling  LMHC courses  COMPENSATION PER COURSE:  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course . This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses meet online.  Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person or online in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use the Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred. This program requires a MA license in School Counseling or LMHC."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Undergraduate-School-of-Education_JREQ-002333": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Undergraduate School of Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-12\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Education is currently seeking individuals to teach the following course beginning in the Fall semester, with classes starting on September 1, 2026 and ending on December 18, 2026: ED222- Culturally Responsive Pedagogy (Time TBD) ED215- Creative Arts in the Early Childhood or Elementary Classrooms (MW 2:00-3:15) COMPENSATION PER COURSE:  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course . This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses meet in-person:  In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday, Wednesday, Friday 50-min block or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-min block. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person or online in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use the Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Banquet-Server--Part-time-_JREQ-002308-2": {
      "title": "Banquet Server (Part-time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-25\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is seeking Full Time Banquet Servers to join their team of dedicated professionals The Wylie Inn & Conference Center employees are part of the Endicott College community and share in the beautiful campus offerings. Endicott is located 20 miles north of Boston and accessible by public transportation. The parking is free and the beautiful beaches are close by! Situated on a picturesque stretch of the Atlantic Coast on Boston’s North Shore, the Wylie Inn and Conference Center at Endicott College offers well appointed, comfortable accommodations with an on-site café restaurant and bar; state of the art IACC certified conference center and an elegant social event venue, upper Manor. The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is ideal for a weekend getaway, retreat or conference. This lush 10-acre inn and conference center is just minutes away from historic downtown Salem, restaurants, scenic Cape Ann, shopping, museums and more.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities   ·        Set up banquet room as instructed by Banquet Captain to include linen, service ware and glassware ·        Attend roll call meetings before events to learn function particulars, including guest and hotel expectations ·        Greet guests and respond to requests in a friendly and courteous manner ·        Serve the food and/or beverage in the order and to the expectation of the Banquet Captain to ensure consistency in the order throughout the banquet ·        Promptly bus dishes as guests complete each course and/or meal at the end of the meal or function   Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Other Duties   ·        Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Food Director with Direct Supervision   Supervisory Responsibilities   No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies   Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·        Minimum 18 years old ·        Ability to work in a standing position for long period of time ·        Ability to lift up to 25 pounds, maneuvering trays of food and drink ·        Ability to work well under pressure in a high-volume event ·        Positive attitude In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay for this position is $18.50 per hour, increasing to $21.50 for Wedding events. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  February 2026 To be considered for this role, please submit an application and include a resume. Please Note: All employees must be 18 years of age or older."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Graduate-Education_JREQ-001541": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Graduate Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-29\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Adjunct faculty are needed for a variety of graduate courses: special education, social emotional learning, leadership and research methodologies. All courses are asynchronous online. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred. Doctorate preferred; Primary expertise in teaching methods and teaching project; Ability to teach content methods courses, introduction to thesis, special education ,social emotional and assessment courses, leadership and research methods."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director-Employer-Relations_JREQ-002690": {
      "title": "Director Employer Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Director of Employer Relations, reporting to the Dean of the Internship & Career Center, will coordinate corporate recruiting efforts and focus on increasing the pool of employers recruiting Endicott students for internships, co-ops, and full-time jobs. The internship strategy will focus on companies interested in hiring interns and co-ops at key regional, national, and international employers, with an emphasis on companies that do significant college recruitment. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .   Key Responsibilities Building Relationships, Employer Outreach and Awareness (40%) ·        Strategically identifies, develops, and maintains employer relationships, locally, nationally, and internationally, to increase full-time job opportunities for students and graduates and internship and co-op opportunities for students. ·        Responsible for global internships and the strategic initiative to grow the program in key countries. Work collaboratively with the International Education Office to grow and promote the program internally and externally. ·        Conduct direct outreach to targeted organizations for increased awareness and visibility of the Endicott College Internship program. ·        Supervise the Graduate Assistant for the Internship & Career Center on daily responsibilities and projects centered around employer engagement, outreach, program development, and marketing of the office and events. Employer Engagement and Recruiting Events (30%) Promotes the College and its graduates to secure job openings and encourages on-campus recruitment activities, including participation in events, information sessions, and class and club presentations. Participates in local, state, and national organizations, including but not limited to chambers of commerce, alumni association events, and professional associations to develop employer relationships and job and internship opportunities.  Organizations include WISE Boston Board Member, Rotary International Engages premier employers through developing on-campus recruiting events including on-campus interviews, class and student club presentations, informational booths, and guest presentations during professional student workshops. Creates opportunities for employer engagement with students for those employers who may not be ready to formally recruit to establish relationships for future opportunities. Examples include: alumni and employer panels, guest speakers in classes, student site visits   Strategic Employer Development and Assessment (25%) Collaborates with deans, faculty, and alumni office to develop leads and targets for outreach. Provides feedback on the design and development of marketing material for employers, including brochures and website content; Conducts ongoing assessment of employer development efforts and provides feedback as to the effectiveness of such efforts. Leads in developing policy, rules, and regulations regarding employer relations operations. Also interprets trends and college-recruiting practices from business and industry in all matters about professional employment. Recommends policies and processes in support of employer relations programs. Work on committees to strengthen and develop the strategic plan and increase branding and awareness of the institution.   5% Professional Development Pursue professional development relevant to student achievement and success responsibilities Other duties as assigned   Community Engagement ●       Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement.   Reporting Structure   ●       Reports to the Dean of the Internship & Career Center. Works under general supervision.   Supervisory Responsibilities ●       No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies ●       Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. ●       Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. ●       Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. ●       Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. ●       Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. ●       Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. ●       Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. ●       Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ●       Bachelor’s Degree ●       5 plus years of professional-level experience in an externally focused position ●       Experience in corporate recruiting/human resources or employer-relations in career services preferred ●       Occasional travel   Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $85,000.00 - $97,000.00 . Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director--Marketing---Advertising_JREQ-002696": {
      "title": "Director, Marketing & Advertising",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Job Summary Working under general supervision of the Assistant Vice President, Communications & Marketing, the Director of Marketing & Advertising serves as a strategic leader within College Communications & Marketing (CCM) and is a key marketing partner to academic and enrollment leaders across Endicott College. The Director develops integrated marketing and advertising strategies that strengthen Endicott’s market position, increase visibility of its undergraduate and graduate academic offerings, and advance institutional enrollment and auxiliary revenue goals.   The Director will lead Endicott’s overarching advertising strategy across digital and traditional channels, ensuring investments are informed by institutional priorities, market conditions, data, and defined measures of success. Another primary responsibility is establishing the strategic foundation for how the College brings its programs to market, including positioning frameworks, audience strategies, value propositions, and campaign plans across advertising, web, print, digital, recruitment communications, and content.   Working closely with the Brand Manager, Undergraduate Admission, the Director of Admission Communication, and the Assistant Vice President of Graduate Enrollment, the Director will help steward undergraduate and graduate enrollment marketing and lead major marketing initiatives from strategy through implementation and assessment.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Outcomes 30 % of Time: Integrated Marketing Strategy & Institutional Priorities ●     Develop and lead annual and long-term marketing strategies that advance College priorities, including enrollment, institutional visibility, engagement, and revenue growth. ●     Serve as a primary marketing partner to leaders across the College, helping identify marketing opportunities, define audiences and objectives, and determine the appropriate strategies and resources to achieve them. ●     Translate institutional goals into actionable marketing plans that establish audiences, positioning, messaging, channels, investment, timelines, and measures of success. ●     Lead marketing strategy for major College initiatives and emerging priorities, bringing together advertising, brand, creative, content, web, social media, and communications as appropriate. ●     Evaluate marketing requests and opportunities against institutional priorities, audience needs, revenue or enrollment potential, available resources, and expected impact. ●     Monitor market conditions, audience behavior, competitive activity, and marketing trends to identify opportunities and inform College marketing strategy. 30% of Time: Advertising, Digital Marketing & Performance ●     Lead Endicott’s advertising strategy across digital and traditional channels, partnering with an external agency on paid search, paid social, and digital display while directly overseeing out-of-home, print, broadcast, and other advertising opportunities. ●     Manage advertising agencies, media partners, vendors, and other external marketing relationships. ●     Establish KPIs and reporting frameworks for major campaigns and regularly communicate performance, insights, and recommendations to College leadership and campus partners. ●     Ensure paid campaigns are supported by strong creative, content, web experiences, and conversion pathways. ●     Evaluate new advertising channels, partnerships, sponsorships, and promotional opportunities based on audience fit, institutional goals, cost, and expected return. 25% of Time: Enrollment & Academic Program Marketing ●     Lead integrated marketing strategy supporting undergraduate and graduate enrollment in close partnership with Enrollment Management and academic leadership. ●     Develop annual undergraduate and graduate marketing plans informed by enrollment goals, priority audiences, market opportunity, program demand, and performance data. ●     Develop marketing strategies for new and priority academic programs, including audience identification, positioning, value propositions, competitive differentiation, launch strategy, and campaign planning. ●     Partner with Undergraduate Admission, Graduate Enrollment, academic leaders, and CCM colleagues to align advertising, recruitment communications, web, print, digital, and content around a cohesive prospective-student journey. ●     Use enrollment and marketing data to identify opportunities and recommend changes to targeting, investment, channels, messaging, creative, and conversion strategies.   15% of Time: Marketing Content, Web & Audience Experience ●     Continually assess whether Endicott has the content, creative assets, web experiences, and audience pathways necessary to support its marketing priorities. ●     Partner with CCM’s creative, social, and web teams to identify gaps and establish priorities for new marketing assets. ●     Partner with CCM’s content, creative, social, video, and photography teams to identify gaps in the College’s marketing asset library and establish priorities for new asset development, with particular attention to priority audiences and programs. ●     Conduct ongoing audits of Endicott’s marketing and enrollment web presence and recommend new pages, landing pages, content improvements, audience pathways, calls to action, and other enhancements. ●     Ensure major advertising and marketing initiatives have the content and digital infrastructure necessary to effectively move audiences from awareness to action. ●     Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. ●     Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure   Reports to the Assistant Vice President of Communications & Marketing.   Supervisory Responsibilities   Supervises the Brand Manager and is responsible for setting priorities, assigning and overseeing work, providing coaching and performance feedback, supporting professional development, conducting performance evaluations, and participating in hiring and onboarding as appropriate.   Core Competencies Strategic Marketing Leadership Connects institutional and enrollment priorities, audience insights, market conditions, and data to develop focused, actionable marketing strategies with clear objectives and measures of success. Consultative Leadership & Partnership Builds credibility and trust with academic, enrollment, and institutional leaders; asks the right questions to uncover underlying needs and opportunities; and translates complex priorities into effective marketing strategies. Audience & Market Orientation Approaches marketing from the perspective of the audience rather than the tactic; uses market research, competitive context, audience behavior, and institutional strengths to inform positioning and strategy. Data-Informed Decision Making Establishes meaningful measures of success, evaluates marketing and advertising performance, identifies actionable insights, and uses data to optimize strategy, investment, channels, and creative. Integrated Thinking Sees how advertising, brand, web, content, communications, enrollment communications, and the prospective-student journey work together; brings the right people and channels together around a shared strategy. Strategic Project Leadership Moves complex initiatives from strategy through execution and assessment; establishes clear objectives, roles, priorities, timelines, and accountability while managing multiple concurrent initiatives effectively. Influence & Communication Communicates strategies, recommendations, and performance insights clearly and persuasively; facilitates productive conversations and can build alignment among stakeholders with different priorities and levels of marketing expertise. Collaborative Leadership Works effectively within a multidisciplinary environment and values the expertise of brand, creative, content, digital, communications, enrollment, and academic colleagues; provides clear strategic direction without unnecessarily owning every aspect of execution. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities ●     Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, business, or a related field required. ●     7+ years of progressively responsible experience in marketing, advertising, or integrated marketing ●     Demonstrated ability to develop comprehensive marketing strategies informed by organizational goals, audience insights, market opportunities, and data. ●     Significant experience developing and managing advertising campaigns across digital and traditional channels, with strong knowledge of paid media, audience targeting, SEO/SEM, conversion strategy, and campaign optimization. ●     Experience developing positioning, audience, value proposition, competitive differentiation, and go-to-market frameworks. ●     Demonstrated ability to establish KPIs, analyze marketing performance, and translate data into actionable recommendations. ●     Experience managing agencies, media partners, vendors, marketing budgets, and complex cross-functional initiatives. ●     Strong consultative, interpersonal, presentation, and communication skills, with demonstrated ability to build trusted relationships across diverse teams and senior leaders. ●     Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of major College events and institutional priorities.   Preferred Qualifications ●     Master's degree preferred ●    Experience in higher education, enrollment marketing, or another complex, mission-driven organization ●    Experience marketing multiple programs, products, services, or audience segments with differing goals and customer journeys. ●    Experience identifying content and creative asset needs and providing strategic direction for video, photography, and other marketing production. ●    Experience working with CRM, marketing automation, analytics, and/or enrollment management platforms. ●    Experience supporting revenue-generating initiatives, events, venues, or other consumer-facing offerings. ●    Experience supervising, mentoring, or developing marketing professionals. ●    Familiarity with higher education enrollment trends, prospective student behavior, and the evolving digital marketing landscape. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $90,000–$100,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  October 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Residence-Director_JREQ-002678": {
      "title": "Assistant Residence Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Under the guidance and supervision of a Residence Director (RD), the Assistant Residence Director (ARD) plays a vital leadership role within the Office of Residence Life. The ARD is responsible for the day-to-day oversight of a residential community, including the supervision and development of a team of Resident Assistants (RAs), supporting a diverse population of students living in Endicott housing, and serving as a conduct hearing officer. This position also participates in an on-call duty rotation, providing crisis response and support for residential students. The ARD is a live-in, full-time, 10-month professional staff position designed for individuals pursuing a Master's degree. The role provides an opportunity for hands-on experience in student affairs and higher education administration while contributing to a supportive, engaging, and inclusive campus community. This position is offered as a three-year term. This live-in role requires the Residence Director (RD) to maintain their primary residence in the assigned on-campus housing as a condition of employment. Housing must be vacated immediately upon separation from the College, regardless of the reason for termination. Key Outcomes 50%:  Residential Community & Supervision Provide direct supervision, training, and performance evaluations for a team of Resident Assistants (RAs) Implement residential education initiatives, including RA-led engagement programming, departmental signature events, and cross-departmental collaborations Support departmental initiatives that foster student engagement, inclusion, and community building in the residential experience Oversee the occupancy management of assigned residential areas, including coordination of check-ins/check-outs, room changes, building and room condition reports (BCRs/RCRs), roommate agreements, safety inspections, and damage billing Assist with broader Residence Life operations such as housing selection, break closings, and summer transition planning 30%:  Student Conduct and On-Call Participate in the on-call duty rotation, providing crisis response for psychological, medical, Title IX, and facilities-related emergencies, and following established College protocols Serve as a conduct hearing officer to address student behavioral concerns and policy violations in accordance with the Office of Community Standards Facilitate conflict resolution and follow-up with students involved in conduct-related matter 20%:  Departmental Initiatives Support Lead and support departmental programming efforts through RA engagement initiatives, signature events, and collaborative programs with other campus offices Promote initiatives that align with the College’s goals around student learning, belonging, and development in the residential setting Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Bachelor’s degree required and preference of candidates who are pursuing a Master’s degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education Administration, or related field. Previous experience in Residence Life and/or Student Affairs highly recommended. Ability and willingness to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends.   Ability to represent Office of Residence Life, and Endicott College in a professional demeanor in person, on the phone and in written correspondences.   Must be energetic and detail oriented with excellent management and organizational skills Must be detail oriented Professional and pleasant manner with outstanding interpersonal and leadership skills is essential In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $ 32,000 - 34,000 . Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Part-Time--Temporary-Medical-Assistants_JREQ-002722": {
      "title": "Part-Time, Temporary Medical Assistants",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Endicott College Wellness Center is establishing a pool of qualified, temporary, part-time Medical Assistants to join our dedicated healthcare team. Reporting directly to the Director of the Wellness Center, candidates selected for this pool will be called on an as-needed basis to cover planned vacations, sick leave, and peak volume times for our full-time staff during the academic year (August 15 – May 30). The Medical Assistants provide clinical and administrative support to nurse practitioners, handling student patient care, vitals, immunizations, and medical records. This is an ideal role for healthcare professionals seeking flexible work opportunities while delivering high-quality, compassionate clinical care to Endicott College students. Advance notice of scheduled shifts will be provided whenever possible. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities ●     25% - Clinical Care: Prepare exam rooms, take vitals (blood pressure, weight), assist with physical exams, and administer vaccines. ●     25% - Student Health Support: Perform point-of-care testing, collect lab specimens (blood/urine), and aid with specialized procedures like splinting or dressing changes. ●     25% - Administrative Duties: Schedule appointments, maintain confidential electronic medical records (EMR), and manage inventory. ●     25% - Patient Interaction: Greet students, document medical histories, and provide care instructions. ●        Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of the Wellness Center and receives functional supervision from Nurse Practitioner staff. Works under general supervision.   Supervisory Responsibilities None   Core Competencies ●       Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. ●       Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. ●       Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. ●       Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. ●       Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. ●       Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. ●       Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. ●       Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ●        High school diploma or equivalent; graduation from an accredited medical assistant program preferred. ●        Certification: Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) or Registered Medical Assistant (RMA) is often required. ●        Experience: Previous experience in a clinic or college health setting is highly desirable, with a focus on working with adolescents and young adults ●        Part-time, on-site position ●        Prior office experiences in a higher education setting ●        Customer service and confidentiality ●        Ability to triage and manage multiple issues and concerns In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $24.00–$29.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  October 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Criminal-Justice--In-Person-_JREQ-002714": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Criminal Justice (In-Person)",
