    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Campus-Shuttle--Van-Driver_JREQ-002715": {
      "title": "Campus Shuttle/ Van Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Campus Shuttle/Van Driver positions report to the Associate Director, Housing Operations in the Residence Life Department. Shuttle drivers are an integral part of supporting student life at Endicott College. Becoming a Campus Shuttle / Van Driver at Endicott College is a fantastic opportunity for local community members or anyone seeking supplemental income with a great schedule. Whether students wish to explore the Beverly area, have access to grocery stores, or to take the train into Boston, Endicott Transportation is about getting the students off-campus and into the community to explore, learn, and embrace the Greater Boston area.   Shuttle service is provided seven days a week. The established routes and shifts are: ●      On-Campus (Mon-Fri) 6am-12pm and 12pm-5pm ●      Off-Campus (Mon-Fri) 7am-12pm (Currently Vacant) and 2pm-7pm ●      Off-Campus (Sat & Sun) 9:45am-2pm (Currently Vacant) and 3:45pm-8pm (Currently Vacant)   These services follow the academic calendar, operating when classes are in session. The Campus Shuttle/Van Driver will not work over break periods including Fall, Winter, Spring, and Summer breaks, as well as school holidays or other campus closures.   Additional shuttle opportunities are available throughout the academic year and over the summer including driving for Misselwood and campus-wide events such as Homecoming, Trustee meetings, and Commencement.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities 100% of Time: Transportation, Operations and Customer Service ●        Provide safe transportation for students, faculty, staff, and guests ●        Maintain a clean, orderly, and safe vehicle environment for all passengers. o   Perform routine vehicle checks and promptly report any mechanical or safety issues to management. ●        Deliver high-quality customer service by welcoming passengers and interacting with a polite, positive, and enthusiastic demeanor. o   Adapt to route changes and respond effectively to on-the-spot passenger requests. o   Maintain a professional appearance o   Maintain clear, concise, and professional communication with passengers, team members, and management. o   Ensure dependability by arriving punctually, fully prepared for all assigned shifts and special events. Community Engagement ●      Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible   Other Duties ●      Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to and w orks under the general supervision of the Associate Director of Housing Operations within the Office of Residence Life.   Supervisory Responsibilities None   Core Competencies   Reliability Shows up on time for shift and finds coverage if necessary Able to get the job done Available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Communication Skills   Has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating with students, faculty/staff, and other guests of the college Delivers information in a timely manner Adaptability/Decision making Shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Is prepared to make decisions independently and in an effective manner Demonstrates sound judgments Follow Through Takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service Anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Is committed to delivering a high standard of customer service Initiative/Personal Leadership Identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Is prepared to make decisions independently and in an effective manner Team Player Shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members   Qualifications and Skills ●      Must have a current and valid driver’s license ●      Good driving record (subject to background check) ●      Excellent customer service oriented communication skills including responding to texts and emails in a timely manner ●      Proven problem-solving ability ●      Communicate effectively with passengers in a customer service role   Preferred Qualifications ●      Previous experience with driving 12+ passenger vehicles   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $17.00–$20.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  October 2026"
    },
