    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Political-Science--In-Person-_JREQ-002695": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Political Science (In-Person)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Adjunct Faculty, Political Science (In-Person)   The School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities at Endicott College is seeking adjunct faculty members with expertise in Political Science. We are especially interested in candidates who have worked in the fields of Foreign Policy or Constitutional Law to teach the following in-person courses during the Spring 2027 semester: American Foreign Policy: Tuesdays and Thursdays, 3:30 PM – 4:45 PM Constitutional Law: Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays, 10:00 AM – 10:50 AM   Key Responsibilities As an adjunct faculty member, you will be expected to: Teach in-person on campus in Beverly, MA. Understand and abide by Endicott's academic policies. Deliver the course according to its description and honor the established learning outcomes. Utilize Canvas as the course's learning management system. Meet all deadlines for roster verification and grade submissions. Communicate proactively with the Associate Dean if issues arise. Meet with students who request assistance or need clarification on course-related matters. Provide samples of student work to be used for assessment purposes. Use your official Endicott email address for all student communications.   Qualifications A Master’s degree is required; a Ph.D. is preferred. Prior college-level teaching experience is strongly preferred.   About Endicott College Come and explore Endicott’s beautiful seaside locale, where employees are an important part of our bustling campus community. We are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and offer free campus parking. We are also highly accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line.   How to Apply If this opportunity looks like the right fit for you, please apply today by submitting your CV and a cover letter. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. KC Choo, Associate Dean of the School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities, at kchoo@endicott.edu. We look forward to hearing from you! In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay for this position is $4,700 per course. This pay reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   Endicott College is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and is committed to the principles of equal employment and complies with all federal, state, and local laws and regulations advancing equal employment. The College's objective is to employ individuals qualified and/or trainable for open positions by virtue of job-related education, training, experience, and qualifications without regard to sex, race, religion, color, age, physical disability, sexual orientation, national or ethnic origin or citizenship, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, or any other status protected by law."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Gerrish-School-of-Business_JREQ-002727": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Gerrish School of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Business is currently seeking individuals to teach the following courses in Spring semester, with classes starting on January 25, 2027 and ending on May 14, 2027 : ACC145 Introduction to Financial and Managerial Accounting BUS249 Introduction to Business Analytics BUS210 Finance BUS375 Financial Modeling COMPENSATION PER COURSE:  Hiring manager to provide a range of adjunct rates for the course for which they are seeking an adjunct. The range would be the lowest for the low-enrolled course to the highest rate paid. (e.g., for a 3 3-credit course: $1,100 - $4,700 depending on enrollment) All courses meet in-person.  Lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week either a Monday/Wednesday/Friday 50-minute format or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-minute format.  Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person or online in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use the Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100- $4,700 per 3-credit course. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Reserve-Campus-Shuttle--Van-Drivers_JREQ-002729": {
      "title": "Reserve Campus Shuttle/ Van Drivers",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Reserve Campus Shuttle/Van Driver positions are part-time, temporary positions reporting to the Associate Director, Housing Operations in the Residence Life Department. The reserve s huttle drivers are an integral part of supporting business operations at Endicott College. Whether driving for a Misselwood wedding, an Admissions event, or the College’s commencement festivities, Endicott Transportation is about engaging and connecting with guests of the College, to leave a positive and lasting impression.   This shuttle service primarily operates when requested by a campus partner. The timing of each event can vary, but a shift is typically between two and eight hours, and can take place on any day of the week, including weekends. Examples include… ●     Misselwood Weddings (Friday, 4pm to 11pm) ●     HR Benefits Fair (Thursday, 11am-3pm) ●     Trustee Meeting (Thursday, 5pm-10pm) ●     Homecoming (Saturday, 7am-6pm) ●     Commencement (Saturday, 7am- 6pm) ●     … and more!   The Associate Director will notify the Reserve Drivers as requests come in and the shifts will be given to staff on a first-come, first-serve basis. There is an expectation that Reserve Campus Shuttle/Van Drivers sign up for at least one shift a semester.   This position may also be asked to fill in for the Campus Shuttle/Van Driver when they are unable to work their scheduled shift.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities   100% of Time: Transportation, Operations and Customer Service ●        Provide safe transportation for students, faculty, staff, and guests ●        Maintain a clean, orderly, and safe vehicle environment for all passengers. o    Perform routine vehicle checks and promptly report any mechanical or safety issues to management. ●        Deliver high-quality customer service by welcoming passengers and interacting with a polite, positive, and enthusiastic demeanor. o    Adapt to route changes and respond effectively to on-the-spot passenger requests. o    Maintain a professional appearance o    Maintain clear, concise, and professional communication with passengers, team members, and management. o    Ensure dependability by arriving punctually, fully prepared for all assigned shifts and special events. Community Engagement ●     Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible   Other Duties ●     Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to and w orks under the general supervision of the Associate Director of Housing Operations within the Office of Residence Life.   Supervisory Responsibilities None   Core Competencies   Reliability Shows up on time for shift and finds coverage if necessary Able to get the job done Available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Communication Skills   Has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating with students, faculty/staff, and other guests of the college Delivers information in a timely manner Adaptability/Decision making Shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Is prepared to make decisions independently and in an effective manner Demonstrates sound judgments Follow Through Takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service Anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Is committed to delivering a high standard of customer service Initiative/Personal Leadership Identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Is prepared to make decisions independently and in an effective manner Team Player Shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members   Qualifications and Skills ●     Must have a current and valid driver’s license ●     Good driving record (subject to background check) ●     Excellent customer service-oriented communication skills including responding to texts and emails in a timely manner ●     Proven problem-solving ability ●     Communicate effectively with passengers in a customer service role   Preferred Qualifications ●     Previous experience with driving 12+ passenger vehicles In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $17.00–$20.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  October 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Strength---Conditioning-and-Gameday-Management_JREQ-002725": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Strength & Conditioning and Gameday Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Job Summary The Assistant Coach, Strength and Conditioning uses a student-athlete first approach which focuses on the physical development and performance of student-athletes, seeks to contribute to the production of athletic teams that the Endicott Community will be proud of, and ensures the athletes are able to attack all of the demands required by collegiate athletics. This is a full-time, 10-month, benefit-eligible position.   Key Outcomes 60 % Create a positive training environment ·         Support a student-athlete first approach ·         Build relationships with each student-athlete ·         Foster a strong work ethic while contributing to the overall development and success of the student-athlete ·         Provide a safe and clean training environment 20% Program design and implementation ·         Utilize science-based information to enhance the athletic ability of the student athlete and teams they work with ·         Effectively collaborate with all athletic performance staff to integrate injury prevention strategies and facilitate efficient rehabilitation, resulting in reduced injury rates and quicker recovery times ·         Practice latest trends and advancements in athletic performance as well as leadership ·         Record and track student-athlete progress ·         Maintain clear and effective verbal and written communication with sport coaches to ensure alignment and collaboration on training goals and strategies 20% Gameday Management: Responsibilities may include multiple duties surrounding athletic events including but not limited to: ·         Welcome the opposing team to campus ·         Escort teams/coaches to locker rooms and playing fields ·         Supervise the student workers at the event ·         Act as site supervisor for the overall operation of an athletics event ·         During championship events, be available for games ·    Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings.   Other duties as required.   Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Coach, Strength & Conditioning. Works under general supervision.   Supervisory Responsibilities None.   Core Competencies   Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills   has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service The employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members     Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Possesses a Bachelor's Degree in Exercise Science or a related field Certified by one or both of the following organizations: NSCA (CSCS) or the CSCCA (SCCC) Certified in CPR/AED  Possesses the ability to lift heavy objects, stand for long periods, work in various environmental conditions. Demonstrates ability to interact effectively with college-age students.   Preferred knowledge and skills: Previous coaching experience in sports and or strength and conditioning  Other certifications that will advance the experience of the Student Athletes such as the United States Weightlifting Certification, Precision Nutrition Certification, and any others that pertain to sport performance.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $44,000–$46,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  October 2026"
    }
  },
